The purpose of this project is to help incorporate new partnerships into ’s Racial Equity and Anti-Racism portfolio. It is anticipated that 15 organizations will be selected to receive grants between $2,500 and $50,000.
These are examples of funding areas of interest within the Racial Equity and Anti-Racism portfolio, although the list is not exhaustive. Project ideas are not limited to this list. We are most interested in ready-to-launch projects rather than planning grants.   

Addressing racism, racial justice, diversity and/or equity: 

In the workplace, educational, professional or civic systems 

In social, media and cultural outlets such as public forums, museum exhibits, publications, podcasts 

To disrupt and dismantle racist cycles AND to replace those cycles with fair and equitable policies, processes and other engagements 

To recruit, cultivate, or train future BIPOC leaders, including mentorship programs 

To put talk into action with social, economic, or cultural impact 

To address and nurture healthy masculinity among BIPOC youth and/or adults  
To rebuild trust between BIPOC communities and local government and to support the process of healing trauma caused by structural racism 

Seed or startup funds to enable and empower fresh, innovative ideas that are ready to launch except for the necessary funding 
